{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Control experiment confirms this is fully independent of any change under review.\n\nRan the exact CI invocation in a worktree at pristine `origin/main` @6f37d9495b with its own venv (verified `rebar` imported from that tree). Result: **1 failed, 12691 passed** — `test_pass_summary_reports_the_decline_count`, the identical single failure, on untouched main.\n\nSo the reproduction does not need a patch under review at all; it just needs the poisoning test to land ahead of the victim on the same xdist worker. Combined with the mechanism in my previous comment (INFO summary dropped at the originating logger while the WARNING per-link record survives) and the 9ac2 precedent fix already applied in the sibling 2b16 file, the one-line change to `caplog.at_level(\"INFO\", logger=apply_records.logger.name)` should close it deterministically."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786613531901778001,"uuid":"4757fa58-f4d6-4e3b-b436-93f2d9aa2923"}